:+1: I've got the same issue.
My workaround: in your doctrine Entity add code to getter, like this:

```
/**
  *@ORM\Entity
  */
class Employee {
...
    /**
     * @var \DateTime $birthday
     * @ORM\Column(type="date", nullable=true)
     */
    private $birthday;
...
    /**
     * Get birthday
     *
     * @return \DateTime 
     */
    public function getBirthday()
    {
        if($this->birthday instanceof \DateTime) {
            $result = clone $this->birthday;
            $result->add(new \DateInterval('PT6H')); // dirty hack to avoid date shift by timezone convertions in my case (GMT+03)
            return $result;
        }
        return $this->birthday;
    }
}
```

:+1:

It's off by X depending on your timezone and if the widget is "single_text".

Controller :

``` php
class DefaultController extends Controller
{
    /**
     * @Route()
     */
    public function indexAction()
    {
        $tz = new \DateTimeZone('Europe/Paris');

        $date1 = new \DateTime('now', $tz);
        $date1->setTime(0, 0, 0);

        $date2 = new \DateTime('now', $tz);
        $date2->setTime(1, 0, 0);

        $data = [
            'date1' => $date1,
            'date2' => $date2,
        ];

        $builder1 = $this->get('form.factory')->createBuilder('form', $data);
        $builder1
            ->add('date1', 'date')
            ->add('date2', 'date')
        ;
        $form1 = $builder1->getForm();

        $builder2 = $this->get('form.factory')->createBuilder('form', $data);
        $builder2
            ->add('date1', 'date', ['widget' => 'single_text'])
            ->add('date2', 'date', ['widget' => 'single_text'])
        ;
        $form2 = $builder2->getForm();

        return $this->render('default/index.html.twig', [
            'form1' => $form1->createView(),
            'form2' => $form2->createView(),
        ]);
    }
}
```

View :

``` twig
{{ form(form1) }}
{{ form(form2) }}
```

Result :

![inputs](https://cloud.githubusercontent.com/assets/1687685/5328755/1b72efe6-7d8d-11e4-9196-ab3daac1a9c6.png)

In "single_text" the view transformer `DateTimeToLocalizedStringTransformer` is applied with UTC input and output. It uses the `\IntlDateFormatter` which is responsible for converting the Timezone in UTC.

Same error, reproduced with this action:

``` php
/**
 * @Route("/")
 * @Template()
 */
public function indexAction()
{
    $data = array(
        'myDateOk'    => new \DateTime('now'),
        'myDateFail'  => new \DateTime(date('Y-m-d')),
    );
    $form = $this->createFormBuilder($data)
        ->add('myDateOk', 'date', array(
            'widget'    => 'single_text',
        ))
        ->add('myDateFail', 'date', array(
            'widget'    => 'single_text',
        ))
        ->getForm()
    ;

    return array(
        'form'          => $form->createView(),
    );
}
```

It also works with `null, null`:

```
$transformer = new \Symfony\Component\Form\Extension\Core\DataTransformer\DateTimeToLocalizedStringTransformer(
        null,
        null,
        \Symfony\Component\Form\Extension\Core\Type\DateType::DEFAULT_FORMAT,
        \IntlDateFormatter::NONE,
        \IntlDateFormatter::GREGORIAN,
        null
    );
    $date = new \DateTime('2014-12-08');
    var_dump($transformer->transform($date));
```

This is because of the inheritance of `DateTimeToLocalizedStringTransformer` from `BaseDateTimeTransformer` where the `__constrcutor` says:

```
$this->inputTimezone = $inputTimezone ?: date_default_timezone_get();
$this->outputTimezone = $outputTimezone ?: date_default_timezone_get(); 
```

